CONTEXT
    Write as a developer explaining work to a capable teammate unfamiliar with the
    feature. Open with the concrete result or problem, then explain behavior, cause,
    and implementation in plain sentences. Introduce internal terms only when useful.
    Explain assumptions. Preserve accurate developer wording and judgments. Avoid
    repetition, generic claims, invented results, personal experience, slang, and
    fake quotations.
AS writing_guidance
